  "review_notes": [
    "The doubled 'ish 'ish is split: the lexical noun (with the supplied existential frame) on the first token, the distributive What ... soever on the second. The reverse assignment is defensible and is named in the unit's note.",
    "there be is the construction's supplied existential frame in a verbless casuistic protasis, so it is not added (rule 20).",
    "The it of the second killeth answers to no morpheme and is added under rule 44."
